{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MLPp2QZg133P2tSe6B9Stu","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t//! Translation of `picoquic/c4.c` — C4 congestion control.\n2\t\n3\tuse crate::PacketContext;\n4\tuse crate::cc_common::{SMOOTHED_LOSS_FACTOR, SMOOTHED_LOSS_SCOPE};\n5\tuse crate::internal::{Connection, Path};\n6\t\n7\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n8\t// Constants from c4.c `#define`s.\n9\t\n10\tconst C4_ALPHA_PUSH_LOW_1024: u64 = 1088; // C: C4_ALPHA_PUSH_LOW_1024 (106.25%)\n11\t/// Gain parameter for the ECN alpha EWMA: g = 1/2^4.  C: `C4_ECN_SHIFT_G`.\n12\tconst C4_ECN_SHIFT_G: u32 = 4;\n13\t\n14\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n15\t// `MULT1024(c, v)` — fixed-point scale by c/1024.  C: `MULT1024`.\n16\t\n17\t#[inline]\n18\tfn mult1024(c: u64, v: u64) -> u64 {\n19\t    (v * c) >> 10\n20\t}\n21\t\n22\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n23\t// Algorithm-state enum.  C: `c4_alg_state_t`.\n24\t\n25\t#[derive(Debug, Copy, Clone, PartialEq, Eq, Default)]\n26\tpub enum C4AlgState {\n27\t    #[default]\n28\t    Initial = 0,\n29\t    Recovery,\n30\t    Cruising,\n31\t    Pushing,\n32\t}\n33\t\n34\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n35\t// Congestion-event discriminant.  C: `c4_congestion_t`.\n36\t\n37\t#[derive(Debug, Copy, Clone, PartialEq, Eq, Default)]\n38\tpub enum C4Congestion {\n39\t    #[default]\n40\t    None = 0,\n41\t    Delay,\n42\t    Ecn,\n43\t    Loss,\n44\t}\n45\t\n46\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n47\t// C4 algorithm state.  C: `c4_state_t` (picoquic/c4.c:143).\n48\t//\n49\t// Type deviations from C:\n50\t//   * single-bit `unsigned int x : 1` bitfields → `bool`\n51\t//   * `const char* option_string` → `Option<String>` (owned copy)\n52\t\n53\tpub struct C4State {\n54\t    pub alg_state: C4AlgState,\n55\t    pub nominal_rate: u64,\n56\t    pub nominal_max_rtt: u64,\n57\t    pub initial_cwnd: u64,\n58\t    pub running_min_rtt: u64,\n59\t    pub alpha_1024_current: u64,\n60\t    pub alpha_1024_previous: u64,\n61\t    pub nb_packets_in_startup: u64,\n62\t    pub era_sequence: u64,\n63\t    pub nb_cruise_left_before_push: u64,\n64\t    pub seed_cwin: u64,\n65\t    pub seed_rate: u64,\n66\t    pub probe_level: i32,\n67\t    pub nb_eras_no_increase: i32,\n68\t    pub push_rate_old: u64,\n69\t    pub push_alpha: u64,\n70\t    pub era_max_rtt: u64,\n71\t    pub era_min_rtt: u64,\n72\t    pub delay_threshold: u64,\n73\t    pub recent_delay_excess: u64,\n74\t    pub last_lost_packet_number: u64,\n75\t    pub smoothed_drop_rate: f64,\n76\t    pub ecn_alpha: u64,\n77\t    pub ecn_ect1: u64,\n78\t    pub ecn_ce: u64,\n79\t    pub ecn_threshold: u64,\n80\t    pub congestion_notified: bool,\n81\t    pub push_was_not_limited: bool,\n82\t    pub use_seed_cwin: bool,\n83\t    pub initial_after_jitter: bool,\n84\t    pub excess_ce_after_push: bool,\n85\t    pub option_string: Option<String>,\n86\t}\n87\t\n88\timpl C4State {\n89\t    /// C: `c4_sensitivity_1024` (picoquic/c4.c:244)\n90\t    ///\n91\t    /// Fixed-point sensitivity in [0, 1024] scaled to `nominal_rate`:\n92\t    /// 0 below 50 kbps, 1024 above 10 Mbps, linearly interpolated in between.\n93\t    fn sensitivity_1024(&self) -> u64 {\n94\t        if self.nominal_rate < 50_000 {\n95\t            0\n96\t        } else if self.nominal_rate > 10_000_000 {\n97\t            1024\n98\t        } else if self.nominal_rate < 1_000_000 {\n99\t            (self.nominal_rate - 50_000) * 963 / 950_000\n100\t        } else {\n101\t            963 + ((self.nominal_rate - 1_000_000) * 61 / 9_000_000)\n102\t        }\n103\t    }\n104\t\n105\t    /// C: `c4_growth_evaluate` (picoquic/c4.c:429)\n106\t    ///\n107\t    /// Returns `true` when the previous era produced meaningful throughput\n108\t    /// growth.  If `push_alpha` was large enough to measure reliably, growth\n109\t    /// is defined as exceeding the alpha-scaled old rate; otherwise it falls\n110\t    /// back to a simple rate comparison guarded by the absence of congestion.\n111\t    fn growth_evaluate(&self) -> bool {\n112\t        if self.push_alpha > C4_ALPHA_PUSH_LOW_1024 {\n113\t            let target_rate =\n114\t                (3 * self.push_rate_old + mult1024(self.push_alpha, self.push_rate_old)) / 4;\n115\t            self.nominal_rate > target_rate\n116\t        } else {\n117\t            self.nominal_rate > self.push_rate_old && !self.congestion_notified\n118\t        }\n119\t    }\n120\t\n121\t    /// C: `c4_growth_reset` (picoquic/c4.c:449)\n122\t    fn growth_reset(&mut self) {\n123\t        self.congestion_notified = false;\n124\t        self.push_was_not_limited = false;\n125\t        self.push_rate_old = self.nominal_rate;\n126\t        // push_alpha is reset to current alpha here; caller sets it to correct\n127\t        // value when entering push state.\n128\t        self.push_alpha = self.alpha_1024_current;\n129\t    }\n130\t\n131\t    /// C: `c4_set_options` (picoquic/c4.c:499)\n132\t    ///\n133\t    /// Parses `option_string` for recognized option characters.  No option\n134\t    /// characters are currently defined; the loop exits on the first unknown.\n135\t    fn set_options(&mut self) {\n136\t        if let Some(s) = self.option_string.as_deref() {\n137\t            // No recognized option characters are currently defined.  The C switch\n138\t            // hits `default: ended = 1` for every character, so the loop exits\n139\t            // immediately after consuming the first character.\n140\t            let _ = s.chars().next();\n141\t        }\n142\t    }\n143\t\n144\t    /// C: `c4_seed_cwin` (picoquic/c4.c:527)\n145\t    pub fn seed_cwin(&mut self, bytes_in_flight: u64) {\n146\t        if self.alg_state == C4AlgState::Initial {\n147\t            self.use_seed_cwin = true;\n148\t            self.seed_cwin = bytes_in_flight;\n149\t        }\n150\t    }\n151\t\n152\t    /// C: `c4_observe` (picoquic/c4.c:1121)\n153\t    ///\n154\t    /// Returns `(cc_state, cc_param)`: the algorithm-state discriminant and\n155\t    /// `nominal_max_rtt`, matching the C convention of filling two `uint64_t*`\n156\t    /// out-params.\n157\t    pub fn observe(&self) -> (u64, u64) {\n158\t        (self.alg_state as u64, self.nominal_max_rtt)\n159\t    }\n160\t\n161\t    /// C: `c4_update_loss_rate` (picoquic/c4.c:301)\n162\t    ///\n163\t    /// Advances the smoothed drop-rate EMA to account for packets up to and\n164\t    /// including `lost_packet_number`.  Each step between the last recorded\n165\t    /// loss and the new one decays the rate; the final step adds one loss\n166\t    /// event.  Steps beyond `SMOOTHED_LOSS_SCOPE` behind the new number are\n167\t    /// skipped to cap the decay loop.\n168\t    pub fn update_loss_rate(&mut self, lost_packet_number: u64) {\n169\t        let mut next_number = self.last_lost_packet_number;\n170\t\n171\t        if lost_packet_number > next_number {\n172\t            if next_number + SMOOTHED_LOSS_SCOPE < lost_packet_number {\n173\t                next_number = lost_packet_number - SMOOTHED_LOSS_SCOPE;\n174\t            }\n175\t\n176\t            while next_number < lost_packet_number {\n177\t                self.smoothed_drop_rate *= 1.0 - SMOOTHED_LOSS_FACTOR;\n178\t                next_number += 1;\n179\t            }\n180\t\n181\t            self.smoothed_drop_rate += (1.0 - self.smoothed_drop_rate) * SMOOTHED_LOSS_FACTOR;\n182\t            self.last_lost_packet_number = lost_packet_number;\n183\t        }\n184\t    }\n185\t\n186\t    /// ECN alpha EWMA core.  C: `c4_update_ecn_alpha` (picoquic/c4.c:321) body.\n187\t    ///\n188\t    /// Takes the current totals directly so the logic can be tested without\n189\t    /// constructing `Path` / `Connection`.  Called by `update_ecn_alpha`.\n190\t    fn ecn_alpha_update_counts(&mut self, ecn_ect1_remote: u64, ecn_ce_remote: u64) {\n191\t        let delta_ect1 = ecn_ect1_remote as i64 - self.ecn_ect1 as i64;\n192\t        let delta_ce = ecn_ce_remote as i64 - self.ecn_ce as i64;\n193\t\n194\t        self.ecn_ect1 = ecn_ect1_remote;\n195\t        self.ecn_ce = ecn_ce_remote;\n196\t\n197\t        if delta_ce > 0 || delta_ect1 > 0 {\n198\t            let sum = delta_ce + delta_ect1;\n199\t            let frac: u64 = if sum > 0 {\n200\t                ((delta_ce * 1024) / sum) as u64\n201\t            } else {\n202\t                0\n203\t            };\n204\t\n205\t            if frac > self.ecn_alpha && frac >= 512 {\n206\t                self.ecn_alpha = frac;\n207\t            } else {\n208\t                // EWMA: alpha = alpha*(1 - 1/2^shift) + frac*(1/2^shift)\n209\t                let alpha_shifted = (self.ecn_alpha << C4_ECN_SHIFT_G) - self.ecn_alpha + frac;\n210\t                self.ecn_alpha = alpha_shifted >> C4_ECN_SHIFT_G;\n211\t            }\n212\t        }\n213\t    }\n214\t\n215\t    /// C: `c4_update_ecn_alpha` (picoquic/c4.c:321)\n216\t    ///\n217\t    /// Selects the right packet context (path-scoped under multipath;\n218\t    /// connection application context otherwise) and delegates to\n219\t    /// `ecn_alpha_update_counts`.\n220\t    #[allow(dead_code)]\n221\t    pub(crate) fn update_ecn_alpha(&mut self, path_x: &Path, connection: &Connection) {\n222\t        let pkt_ctx = if connection.is_multipath_enabled {\n223\t            &path_x.pkt_ctx\n224\t        } else {\n225\t            &connection.pkt_ctx[PacketContext::Application as usize]\n226\t        };\n227\t        self.ecn_alpha_update_counts(pkt_ctx.ecn_ect1_total_remote, pkt_ctx.ecn_ce_total_remote);\n228\t    }\n229\t}\n230\t\n231\t#[cfg(test)]\n232\tmod tests {\n233\t    use super::*;\n234\t\n235\t    fn make_state() -> C4State {\n236\t        C4State {\n237\t            alg_state: C4AlgState::default(),\n238\t            nominal_rate: 0,\n239\t            nominal_max_rtt: 0,\n240\t            initial_cwnd: 0,\n241\t            running_min_rtt: 0,\n242\t            alpha_1024_current: 0,\n243\t            alpha_1024_previous: 0,\n244\t            nb_packets_in_startup: 0,\n245\t            era_sequence: 0,\n246\t            nb_cruise_left_before_push: 0,\n247\t            seed_cwin: 0,\n248\t            seed_rate: 0,\n249\t            probe_level: 0,\n250\t            nb_eras_no_increase: 0,\n251\t            push_rate_old: 0,\n252\t            push_alpha: 0,\n253\t            era_max_rtt: 0,\n254\t            era_min_rtt: 0,\n255\t            delay_threshold: 0,\n256\t            recent_delay_excess: 0,\n257\t            last_lost_packet_number: 0,\n258\t            smoothed_drop_rate: 0.0,\n259\t            ecn_alpha: 0,\n260\t            ecn_ect1: 0,\n261\t            ecn_ce: 0,\n262\t            ecn_threshold: 0,\n263\t            congestion_notified: false,\n264\t            push_was_not_limited: false,\n265\t            use_seed_cwin: false,\n266\t            initial_after_jitter: false,\n267\t            excess_ce_after_push: false,\n268\t            option_string: None,\n269\t        }\n270\t    }\n271\t\n272\t    #[test]\n273\t    fn growth_evaluate_high_alpha_growing() {\n274\t        let mut s = make_state();\n275\t        // push_alpha > 1088, push_rate_old = 1000, nominal_rate must exceed:\n276\t        // target = (3*1000 + MULT1024(1280, 1000)) / 4 = (3000 + 1250) / 4 = 1062\n277\t        s.push_alpha = 1280;\n278\t        s.push_rate_old = 1000;\n279\t        s.nominal_rate = 1100;\n280\t        assert!(s.growth_evaluate());\n281\t    }\n282\t\n283\t    #[test]\n284\t    fn growth_evaluate_high_alpha_not_growing() {\n285\t        let mut s = make_state();\n286\t        s.push_alpha = 1280;\n287\t        s.push_rate_old = 1000;\n288\t        s.nominal_rate = 1000; // equal to target_rate or below\n289\t        assert!(!s.growth_evaluate());\n290\t    }\n291\t\n292\t    #[test]\n293\t    fn growth_evaluate_low_alpha_growing_no_congestion() {\n294\t        let mut s = make_state();\n295\t        s.push_alpha = 1000; // <= 1088\n296\t        s.push_rate_old = 800;\n297\t        s.nominal_rate = 900;\n298\t        s.congestion_notified = false;\n299\t        assert!(s.growth_evaluate());\n300\t    }\n301\t\n302\t    #[test]\n303\t    fn growth_evaluate_low_alpha_congestion_blocks_growth() {\n304\t        let mut s = make_state();\n305\t        s.push_alpha = 1000;\n306\t        s.push_rate_old = 800;\n307\t        s.nominal_rate = 900;\n308\t        s.congestion_notified = true;\n309\t        assert!(!s.growth_evaluate());\n310\t    }\n311\t\n312\t    // --- sensitivity_1024 ---\n313\t\n314\t    #[test]\n315\t    fn sensitivity_below_50k() {\n316\t        let mut s = make_state();\n317\t        s.nominal_rate = 49_999;\n318\t        assert_eq!(s.sensitivity_1024(), 0);\n319\t    }\n320\t\n321\t    #[test]\n322\t    fn sensitivity_at_50k_boundary() {\n323\t        let mut s = make_state();\n324\t        s.nominal_rate = 50_000;\n325\t        // (50000 - 50000) * 963 / 950000 == 0\n326\t        assert_eq!(s.sensitivity_1024(), 0);\n327\t    }\n328\t\n329\t    #[test]\n330\t    fn sensitivity_midrange() {\n331\t        let mut s = make_state();\n332\t        s.nominal_rate = 500_000;\n333\t        // (500000 - 50000) * 963 / 950000 = 450000 * 963 / 950000 = 456\n334\t        assert_eq!(s.sensitivity_1024(), 456);\n335\t    }\n336\t\n337\t    #[test]\n338\t    fn sensitivity_at_1mbps() {\n339\t        let mut s = make_state();\n340\t        s.nominal_rate = 1_000_000;\n341\t        // hits else branch: 963 + (0 * 61 / 9000000) = 963\n342\t        assert_eq!(s.sensitivity_1024(), 963);\n343\t    }\n344\t\n345\t    #[test]\n346\t    fn sensitivity_at_10mbps() {\n347\t        let mut s = make_state();\n348\t        s.nominal_rate = 10_000_000;\n349\t        // 963 + (9000000 * 61 / 9000000) = 963 + 61 = 1024\n350\t        assert_eq!(s.sensitivity_1024(), 1024);\n351\t    }\n352\t\n353\t    #[test]\n354\t    fn sensitivity_above_10mbps() {\n355\t        let mut s = make_state();\n356\t        s.nominal_rate = 10_000_001;\n357\t        assert_eq!(s.sensitivity_1024(), 1024);\n358\t    }\n359\t\n360\t    // --- growth_reset ---\n361\t\n362\t    #[test]\n363\t    fn growth_reset_clears_flags_and_snapshots() {\n364\t        let mut s = make_state();\n365\t        s.nominal_rate = 5_000_000;\n366\t        s.alpha_1024_current = 1100;\n367\t        s.congestion_notified = true;\n368\t        s.push_was_not_limited = true;\n369\t        s.push_rate_old = 1_000_000;\n370\t        s.push_alpha = 900;\n371\t\n372\t        s.growth_reset();\n373\t\n374\t        assert!(!s.congestion_notified);\n375\t        assert!(!s.push_was_not_limited);\n376\t        assert_eq!(s.push_rate_old, 5_000_000);\n377\t        assert_eq!(s.push_alpha, 1100);\n378\t    }\n379\t\n380\t    // --- set_options ---\n381\t\n382\t    #[test]\n383\t    fn set_options_none_is_noop() {\n384\t        let mut s = make_state();\n385\t        s.option_string = None;\n386\t        s.set_options(); // must not panic\n387\t    }\n388\t\n389\t    #[test]\n390\t    fn set_options_unknown_chars_are_noop() {\n391\t        let mut s = make_state();\n392\t        s.option_string = Some(\"xyz\".to_owned());\n393\t        s.set_options(); // must not panic; no state change expected\n394\t    }\n395\t\n396\t    // --- seed_cwin ---\n397\t\n398\t    #[test]\n399\t    fn seed_cwin_sets_when_initial() {\n400\t        let mut s = make_state();\n401\t        s.alg_state = C4AlgState::Initial;\n402\t        s.seed_cwin(123_456);\n403\t        assert!(s.use_seed_cwin);\n404\t        assert_eq!(s.seed_cwin, 123_456);\n405\t    }\n406\t\n407\t    #[test]\n408\t    fn seed_cwin_ignored_when_not_initial() {\n409\t        let mut s = make_state();\n410\t        s.alg_state = C4AlgState::Cruising;\n411\t        s.seed_cwin(123_456);\n412\t        assert!(!s.use_seed_cwin);\n413\t        assert_eq!(s.seed_cwin, 0);\n414\t    }\n415\t\n416\t    // --- observe ---\n417\t\n418\t    #[test]\n419\t    fn observe_returns_state_and_rtt() {\n420\t        let mut s = make_state();\n421\t        s.alg_state = C4AlgState::Pushing;\n422\t        s.nominal_max_rtt = 42_000;\n423\t        let (cc_state, cc_param) = s.observe();\n424\t        assert_eq!(cc_state, C4AlgState::Pushing as u64);\n425\t        assert_eq!(cc_param, 42_000);\n426\t    }\n427\t\n428\t    #[test]\n429\t    fn observe_initial_state() {\n430\t        let s = make_state();\n431\t        let (cc_state, cc_param) = s.observe();\n432\t        assert_eq!(cc_state, 0); // C4AlgState::Initial == 0\n433\t        assert_eq!(cc_param, 0);\n434\t    }\n435\t\n436\t    // --- update_loss_rate ---\n437\t\n438\t    #[test]\n439\t    fn loss_rate_no_update_when_not_newer() {\n440\t        let mut s = make_state();\n441\t        s.last_lost_packet_number = 100;\n442\t        s.smoothed_drop_rate = 0.5;\n443\t        s.update_loss_rate(100); // same number → no change\n444\t        assert_eq!(s.smoothed_drop_rate, 0.5);\n445\t        assert_eq!(s.last_lost_packet_number, 100);\n446\t    }\n447\t\n448\t    #[test]\n449\t    fn loss_rate_single_step() {\n450\t        let mut s = make_state();\n451\t        s.last_lost_packet_number = 0;\n452\t        s.smoothed_drop_rate = 0.0;\n453\t        s.update_loss_rate(1);\n454\t        // one decay step: rate *= (1 - 1/16) = 0  (was 0)\n455\t        // then: rate += (1 - 0) * (1/16) = 1/16\n456\t        assert!((s.smoothed_drop_rate - 1.0 / 16.0).abs() < 1e-12);\n457\t        assert_eq!(s.last_lost_packet_number, 1);\n458\t    }\n459\t\n460\t    #[test]\n461\t    fn loss_rate_caps_scope() {\n462\t        let mut s = make_state();\n463\t        // Gap far exceeds SMOOTHED_LOSS_SCOPE=32; loop should start at\n464\t        // lost_packet_number - 32 so only 32 decays happen, not 1000.\n465\t        s.last_lost_packet_number = 0;\n466\t        s.smoothed_drop_rate = 1.0;\n467\t        s.update_loss_rate(1000);\n468\t        // After 32 decay steps: 1.0 * (15/16)^32 ≈ 0.1209\n469\t        // Then one more step adding the loss event:\n470\t        // result = decayed + (1 - decayed) * (1/16)\n471\t        let expected_decayed = (15.0f64 / 16.0).powi(32);\n472\t        let expected = expected_decayed + (1.0 - expected_decayed) * (1.0 / 16.0);\n473\t        assert!((s.smoothed_drop_rate - expected).abs() < 1e-9);\n474\t        assert_eq!(s.last_lost_packet_number, 1000);\n475\t    }\n476\t\n477\t    // --- ecn_alpha_update_counts ---\n478\t\n479\t    #[test]\n480\t    fn ecn_alpha_no_update_when_both_zero_delta() {\n481\t        let mut s = make_state();\n482\t        s.ecn_alpha = 500;\n483\t        s.ecn_ect1 = 100;\n484\t        s.ecn_ce = 50;\n485\t        // same totals → no delta → alpha unchanged\n486\t        s.ecn_alpha_update_counts(100, 50);\n487\t        assert_eq!(s.ecn_alpha, 500);\n488\t    }\n489\t\n490\t    #[test]\n491\t    fn ecn_alpha_fast_path_large_frac() {\n492\t        let mut s = make_state();\n493\t        s.ecn_alpha = 400;\n494\t        s.ecn_ect1 = 0;\n495\t        s.ecn_ce = 0;\n496\t        // delta_ce = 600, delta_ect1 = 400 → frac = 600*1024/(600+400) = 614\n497\t        // frac (614) > alpha (400) and frac >= 512 → fast path: alpha = frac\n498\t        s.ecn_alpha_update_counts(400, 600);\n499\t        assert_eq!(s.ecn_alpha, 614);\n500\t    }\n501\t\n502\t    #[test]\n503\t    fn ecn_alpha_ewma_path() {\n504\t        let mut s = make_state();\n505\t        s.ecn_alpha = 256;\n506\t        s.ecn_ect1 = 0;\n507\t        s.ecn_ce = 0;\n508\t        // delta_ce = 100, delta_ect1 = 900 → frac = 100*1024/1000 = 102\n509\t        // frac (102) < alpha (256) → EWMA path\n510\t        // alpha_shifted = 256 * 16 - 256 + 102 = 256*15 + 102 = 3840 + 102 = 3942\n511\t        // new alpha = 3942 / 16 = 246\n512\t        s.ecn_alpha_update_counts(900, 100);\n513\t        assert_eq!(s.ecn_alpha, 246);\n514\t    }\n515\t\n516\t    #[test]\n517\t    fn ecn_alpha_only_ect1_delta() {\n518\t        let mut s = make_state();\n519\t        s.ecn_alpha = 200;\n520\t        s.ecn_ect1 = 0;\n521\t        s.ecn_ce = 0;\n522\t        // delta_ect1 = 500, delta_ce = 0 → frac = 0\n523\t        // frac (0) < alpha (200) → EWMA:\n524\t        //   alpha_shifted = 200 << 4 = 3200; 3200 - 200 = 3000; 3000 + 0 = 3000\n525\t        //   new alpha = 3000 >> 4 = 187\n526\t        s.ecn_alpha_update_counts(500, 0);\n527\t        assert_eq!(s.ecn_alpha, 187);\n528\t    }\n529\t}\n530\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"36feb9dd-a64c-482f-8d2d-3dfde6f4c9e3","uuid":"45925afc-bab9-42da-8187-04abd8213694","timestamp":"2026-05-07T13:38:39.634Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/richbarn/Projects/picoquic/rs/fq/src/c4.rs","content":"//! Translation of `picoquic/c4.c` — C4 congestion control.\n\nuse crate::PacketContext;\nuse crate::cc_common::{SMOOTHED_LOSS_FACTOR, SMOOTHED_LOSS_SCOPE};\nuse crate::internal::{Connection, Path};\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Constants from c4.c `#define`s.\n\nconst C4_ALPHA_PUSH_LOW_1024: u64 = 1088; // C: C4_ALPHA_PUSH_LOW_1024 (106.25%)\n/// Gain parameter for the ECN alpha EWMA: g = 1/2^4.  C: `C4_ECN_SHIFT_G`.\nconst C4_ECN_SHIFT_G: u32 = 4;\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// `MULT1024(c, v)` — fixed-point scale by c/1024.  C: `MULT1024`.\n\n#[inline]\nfn mult1024(c: u64, v: u64) -> u64 {\n    (v * c) >> 10\n}\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Algorithm-state enum.  C: `c4_alg_state_t`.\n\n#[derive(Debug, Copy, Clone, PartialEq, Eq, Default)]\npub enum C4AlgState {\n    #[default]\n    Initial = 0,\n    Recovery,\n    Cruising,\n    Pushing,\n}\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// Congestion-event discriminant.  C: `c4_congestion_t`.\n\n#[derive(Debug, Copy, Clone, PartialEq, Eq, Default)]\npub enum C4Congestion {\n    #[default]\n    None = 0,\n    Delay,\n    Ecn,\n    Loss,\n}\n\n// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n// C4 algorithm state.  C: `c4_state_t` (picoquic/c4.c:143).\n//\n// Type deviations from C:\n//   * single-bit `unsigned int x : 1` bitfields → `bool`\n//   * `const char* option_string` → `Option<String>` (owned copy)\n\npub struct C4State {\n    pub alg_state: C4AlgState,\n    pub nominal_rate: u64,\n    pub nominal_max_rtt: u64,\n    pub initial_cwnd: u64,\n    pub running_min_rtt: u64,\n    pub alpha_1024_current: u64,\n    pub alpha_1024_previous: u64,\n    pub nb_packets_in_startup: u64,\n    pub era_sequence: u64,\n    pub nb_cruise_left_before_push: u64,\n    pub seed_cwin: u64,\n    pub seed_rate: u64,\n    pub probe_level: i32,\n    pub nb_eras_no_increase: i32,\n    pub push_rate_old: u64,\n    pub push_alpha: u64,\n    pub era_max_rtt: u64,\n    pub era_min_rtt: u64,\n    pub delay_threshold: u64,\n    pub recent_delay_excess: u64,\n    pub last_lost_packet_number: u64,\n    pub smoothed_drop_rate: f64,\n    pub ecn_alpha: u64,\n    pub ecn_ect1: u64,\n    pub ecn_ce: u64,\n    pub ecn_threshold: u64,\n    pub congestion_notified: bool,\n    pub push_was_not_limited: bool,\n    pub use_seed_cwin: bool,\n    pub initial_after_jitter: bool,\n    pub excess_ce_after_push: bool,\n    pub option_string: Option<String>,\n}\n\nimpl C4State {\n    /// C: `c4_sensitivity_1024` (picoquic/c4.c:244)\n    ///\n    /// Fixed-point sensitivity in [0, 1024] scaled to `nominal_rate`:\n    /// 0 below 50 kbps, 1024 above 10 Mbps, linearly interpolated in between.\n    fn sensitivity_1024(&self) -> u64 {\n        if self.nominal_rate < 50_000 {\n            0\n        } else if self.nominal_rate > 10_000_000 {\n            1024\n        } else if self.nominal_rate < 1_000_000 {\n            (self.nominal_rate - 50_000) * 963 / 950_000\n        } else {\n            963 + ((self.nominal_rate - 1_000_000) * 61 / 9_000_000)\n        }\n    }\n\n    /// C: `c4_growth_evaluate` (picoquic/c4.c:429)\n    ///\n    /// Returns `true` when the previous era produced meaningful throughput\n    /// growth.  If `push_alpha` was large enough to measure reliably, growth\n    /// is defined as exceeding the alpha-scaled old rate; otherwise it falls\n    /// back to a simple rate comparison guarded by the absence of congestion.\n    fn growth_evaluate(&self) -> bool {\n        if self.push_alpha > C4_ALPHA_PUSH_LOW_1024 {\n            let target_rate =\n                (3 * self.push_rate_old + mult1024(self.push_alpha, self.push_rate_old)) / 4;\n            self.nominal_rate > target_rate\n        } else {\n            self.nominal_rate > self.push_rate_old && !self.congestion_notified\n        }\n    }\n\n    /// C: `c4_growth_reset` (picoquic/c4.c:449)\n    fn growth_reset(&mut self) {\n        self.congestion_notified = false;\n        self.push_was_not_limited = false;\n        self.push_rate_old = self.nominal_rate;\n        // push_alpha is reset to current alpha here; caller sets it to correct\n        // value when entering push state.\n        self.push_alpha = self.alpha_1024_current;\n    }\n\n    /// C: `c4_set_options` (picoquic/c4.c:499)\n    ///\n    /// Parses `option_string` for recognized option characters.  No option\n    /// characters are currently defined; the loop exits on the first unknown.\n    fn set_options(&mut self) {\n        if let Some(s) = self.option_string.as_deref() {\n            // No recognized option characters are currently defined.  The C switch\n            // hits `default: ended = 1` for every character, so the loop exits\n            // immediately after consuming the first character.\n            let _ = s.chars().next();\n        }\n    }\n\n    /// C: `c4_seed_cwin` (picoquic/c4.c:527)\n    pub fn seed_cwin(&mut self, bytes_in_flight: u64) {\n        if self.alg_state == C4AlgState::Initial {\n            self.use_seed_cwin = true;\n            self.seed_cwin = bytes_in_flight;\n        }\n    }\n\n    /// C: `c4_observe` (picoquic/c4.c:1121)\n    ///\n    /// Returns `(cc_state, cc_param)`: the algorithm-state discriminant and\n    /// `nominal_max_rtt`, matching the C convention of filling two `uint64_t*`\n    /// out-params.\n    pub fn observe(&self) -> (u64, u64) {\n        (self.alg_state as u64, self.nominal_max_rtt)\n    }\n\n    /// C: `c4_update_loss_rate` (picoquic/c4.c:301)\n    ///\n    /// Advances the smoothed drop-rate EMA to account for packets up to and\n    /// including `lost_packet_number`.  Each step between the last recorded\n    /// loss and the new one decays the rate; the final step adds one loss\n    /// event.  Steps beyond `SMOOTHED_LOSS_SCOPE` behind the new number are\n    /// skipped to cap the decay loop.\n    pub fn update_loss_rate(&mut self, lost_packet_number: u64) {\n        let mut next_number = self.last_lost_packet_number;\n\n        if lost_packet_number > next_number {\n            if next_number + SMOOTHED_LOSS_SCOPE < lost_packet_number {\n                next_number = lost_packet_number - SMOOTHED_LOSS_SCOPE;\n            }\n\n            while next_number < lost_packet_number {\n                self.smoothed_drop_rate *= 1.0 - SMOOTHED_LOSS_FACTOR;\n                next_number += 1;\n            }\n\n            self.smoothed_drop_rate += (1.0 - self.smoothed_drop_rate) * SMOOTHED_LOSS_FACTOR;\n            self.last_lost_packet_number = lost_packet_number;\n        }\n    }\n\n    /// ECN alpha EWMA core.  C: `c4_update_ecn_alpha` (picoquic/c4.c:321) body.\n    ///\n    /// Takes the current totals directly so the logic can be tested without\n    /// constructing `Path` / `Connection`.  Called by `update_ecn_alpha`.\n    fn ecn_alpha_update_counts(&mut self, ecn_ect1_remote: u64, ecn_ce_remote: u64) {\n        let delta_ect1 = ecn_ect1_remote as i64 - self.ecn_ect1 as i64;\n        let delta_ce = ecn_ce_remote as i64 - self.ecn_ce as i64;\n\n        self.ecn_ect1 = ecn_ect1_remote;\n        self.ecn_ce = ecn_ce_remote;\n\n        if delta_ce > 0 || delta_ect1 > 0 {\n            let sum = delta_ce + delta_ect1;\n            let frac: u64 = if sum > 0 {\n                ((delta_ce * 1024) / sum) as u64\n            } else {\n                0\n            };\n\n            if frac > self.ecn_alpha && frac >= 512 {\n                self.ecn_alpha = frac;\n            } else {\n                // EWMA: alpha = alpha*(1 - 1/2^shift) + frac*(1/2^shift)\n                let alpha_shifted = (self.ecn_alpha << C4_ECN_SHIFT_G) - self.ecn_alpha + frac;\n                self.ecn_alpha = alpha_shifted >> C4_ECN_SHIFT_G;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    /// C: `c4_update_ecn_alpha` (picoquic/c4.c:321)\n    ///\n    /// Selects the right packet context (path-scoped under multipath;\n    /// connection application context otherwise) and delegates to\n    /// `ecn_alpha_update_counts`.\n    #[allow(dead_code)]\n    pub(crate) fn update_ecn_alpha(&mut self, path_x: &Path, connection: &Connection) {\n        let pkt_ctx = if connection.is_multipath_enabled {\n            &path_x.pkt_ctx\n        } else {\n            &connection.pkt_ctx[PacketContext::Application as usize]\n        };\n        self.ecn_alpha_update_counts(pkt_ctx.ecn_ect1_total_remote, pkt_ctx.ecn_ce_total_remote);\n    }\n}\n\n#[cfg(test)]\nmod tests {\n    use super::*;\n\n    fn make_state() -> C4State {\n        C4State {\n            alg_state: C4AlgState::default(),\n            nominal_rate: 0,\n            nominal_max_rtt: 0,\n            initial_cwnd: 0,\n            running_min_rtt: 0,\n            alpha_1024_current: 0,\n            alpha_1024_previous: 0,\n            nb_packets_in_startup: 0,\n            era_sequence: 0,\n            nb_cruise_left_before_push: 0,\n            seed_cwin: 0,\n            seed_rate: 0,\n            probe_level: 0,\n            nb_eras_no_increase: 0,\n            push_rate_old: 0,\n            push_alpha: 0,\n            era_max_rtt: 0,\n            era_min_rtt: 0,\n            delay_threshold: 0,\n            recent_delay_excess: 0,\n            last_lost_packet_number: 0,\n            smoothed_drop_rate: 0.0,\n            ecn_alpha: 0,\n            ecn_ect1: 0,\n            ecn_ce: 0,\n            ecn_threshold: 0,\n            congestion_notified: false,\n            push_was_not_limited: false,\n            use_seed_cwin: false,\n            initial_after_jitter: false,\n            excess_ce_after_push: false,\n            option_string: None,\n        }\n    }\n\n    #[test]\n    fn growth_evaluate_high_alpha_growing() {\n        let mut s = make_state();\n        // push_alpha > 1088, push_rate_old = 1000, nominal_rate must exceed:\n        // target = (3*1000 + MULT1024(1280, 1000)) / 4 = (3000 + 1250) / 4 = 1062\n        s.push_alpha = 1280;\n        s.push_rate_old = 1000;\n        s.nominal_rate = 1100;\n        assert!(s.growth_evaluate());\n    }\n\n    #[test]\n    fn growth_evaluate_high_alpha_not_growing() {\n        let mut s = make_state();\n        s.push_alpha = 1280;\n        s.push_rate_old = 1000;\n        s.nominal_rate = 1000; // equal to target_rate or below\n        assert!(!s.growth_evaluate());\n    }\n\n    #[test]\n    fn growth_evaluate_low_alpha_growing_no_congestion() {\n        let mut s = make_state();\n        s.push_alpha = 1000; // <= 1088\n        s.push_rate_old = 800;\n        s.nominal_rate = 900;\n        s.congestion_notified = false;\n        assert!(s.growth_evaluate());\n    }\n\n    #[test]\n    fn growth_evaluate_low_alpha_congestion_blocks_growth() {\n        let mut s = make_state();\n        s.push_alpha = 1000;\n        s.push_rate_old = 800;\n        s.nominal_rate = 900;\n        s.congestion_notified = true;\n        assert!(!s.growth_evaluate());\n    }\n\n    // --- sensitivity_1024 ---\n\n    #[test]\n    fn sensitivity_below_50k() {\n        let mut s = make_state();\n        s.nominal_rate = 49_999;\n        assert_eq!(s.sensitivity_1024(), 0);\n    }\n\n    #[test]\n    fn sensitivity_at_50k_boundary() {\n        let mut s = make_state();\n        s.nominal_rate = 50_000;\n        // (50000 - 50000) * 963 / 950000 == 0\n        assert_eq!(s.sensitivity_1024(), 0);\n    }\n\n    #[test]\n    fn sensitivity_midrange() {\n        let mut s = make_state();\n        s.nominal_rate = 500_000;\n        // (500000 - 50000) * 963 / 950000 = 450000 * 963 / 950000 = 456\n        assert_eq!(s.sensitivity_1024(), 456);\n    }\n\n    #[test]\n    fn sensitivity_at_1mbps() {\n        let mut s = make_state();\n        s.nominal_rate = 1_000_000;\n        // hits else branch: 963 + (0 * 61 / 9000000) = 963\n        assert_eq!(s.sensitivity_1024(), 963);\n    }\n\n    #[test]\n    fn sensitivity_at_10mbps() {\n        let mut s = make_state();\n        s.nominal_rate = 10_000_000;\n        // 963 + (9000000 * 61 / 9000000) = 963 + 61 = 1024\n        assert_eq!(s.sensitivity_1024(), 1024);\n    }\n\n    #[test]\n    fn sensitivity_above_10mbps() {\n        let mut s = make_state();\n        s.nominal_rate = 10_000_001;\n        assert_eq!(s.sensitivity_1024(), 1024);\n    }\n\n    // --- growth_reset ---\n\n    #[test]\n    fn growth_reset_clears_flags_and_snapshots() {\n        let mut s = make_state();\n        s.nominal_rate = 5_000_000;\n        s.alpha_1024_current = 1100;\n        s.congestion_notified = true;\n        s.push_was_not_limited = true;\n        s.push_rate_old = 1_000_000;\n        s.push_alpha = 900;\n\n        s.growth_reset();\n\n        assert!(!s.congestion_notified);\n        assert!(!s.push_was_not_limited);\n        assert_eq!(s.push_rate_old, 5_000_000);\n        assert_eq!(s.push_alpha, 1100);\n    }\n\n    // --- set_options ---\n\n    #[test]\n    fn set_options_none_is_noop() {\n        let mut s = make_state();\n        s.option_string = None;\n        s.set_options(); // must not panic\n    }\n\n    #[test]\n    fn set_options_unknown_chars_are_noop() {\n        let mut s = make_state();\n        s.option_string = Some(\"xyz\".to_owned());\n        s.set_options(); // must not panic; no state change expected\n    }\n\n    // --- seed_cwin ---\n\n    #[test]\n    fn seed_cwin_sets_when_initial() {\n        let mut s = make_state();\n        s.alg_state = C4AlgState::Initial;\n        s.seed_cwin(123_456);\n        assert!(s.use_seed_cwin);\n        assert_eq!(s.seed_cwin, 123_456);\n    }\n\n    #[test]\n    fn seed_cwin_ignored_when_not_initial() {\n        let mut s = make_state();\n        s.alg_state = C4AlgState::Cruising;\n        s.seed_cwin(123_456);\n        assert!(!s.use_seed_cwin);\n        assert_eq!(s.seed_cwin, 0);\n    }\n\n    // --- observe ---\n\n    #[test]\n    fn observe_returns_state_and_rtt() {\n        let mut s = make_state();\n        s.alg_state = C4AlgState::Pushing;\n        s.nominal_max_rtt = 42_000;\n        let (cc_state, cc_param) = s.observe();\n        assert_eq!(cc_state, C4AlgState::Pushing as u64);\n        assert_eq!(cc_param, 42_000);\n    }\n\n    #[test]\n    fn observe_initial_state() {\n        let s = make_state();\n        let (cc_state, cc_param) = s.observe();\n        assert_eq!(cc_state, 0); // C4AlgState::Initial == 0\n        assert_eq!(cc_param, 0);\n    }\n\n    // --- update_loss_rate ---\n\n    #[test]\n    fn loss_rate_no_update_when_not_newer() {\n        let mut s = make_state();\n        s.last_lost_packet_number = 100;\n        s.smoothed_drop_rate = 0.5;\n        s.update_loss_rate(100); // same number → no change\n        assert_eq!(s.smoothed_drop_rate, 0.5);\n        assert_eq!(s.last_lost_packet_number, 100);\n    }\n\n    #[test]\n    fn loss_rate_single_step() {\n        let mut s = make_state();\n        s.last_lost_packet_number = 0;\n        s.smoothed_drop_rate = 0.0;\n        s.update_loss_rate(1);\n        // one decay step: rate *= (1 - 1/16) = 0  (was 0)\n        // then: rate += (1 - 0) * (1/16) = 1/16\n        assert!((s.smoothed_drop_rate - 1.0 / 16.0).abs() < 1e-12);\n        assert_eq!(s.last_lost_packet_number, 1);\n    }\n\n    #[test]\n    fn loss_rate_caps_scope() {\n        let mut s = make_state();\n        // Gap far exceeds SMOOTHED_LOSS_SCOPE=32; loop should start at\n        // lost_packet_number - 32 so only 32 decays happen, not 1000.\n        s.last_lost_packet_number = 0;\n        s.smoothed_drop_rate = 1.0;\n        s.update_loss_rate(1000);\n        // After 32 decay steps: 1.0 * (15/16)^32 ≈ 0.1209\n        // Then one more step adding the loss event:\n        // result = decayed + (1 - decayed) * (1/16)\n        let expected_decayed = (15.0f64 / 16.0).powi(32);\n        let expected = expected_decayed + (1.0 - expected_decayed) * (1.0 / 16.0);\n        assert!((s.smoothed_drop_rate - expected).abs() < 1e-9);\n        assert_eq!(s.last_lost_packet_number, 1000);\n    }\n\n    // --- ecn_alpha_update_counts ---\n\n    #[test]\n    fn ecn_alpha_no_update_when_both_zero_delta() {\n        let mut s = make_state();\n        s.ecn_alpha = 500;\n        s.ecn_ect1 = 100;\n        s.ecn_ce = 50;\n        // same totals → no delta → alpha unchanged\n        s.ecn_alpha_update_counts(100, 50);\n        assert_eq!(s.ecn_alpha, 500);\n    }\n\n    #[test]\n    fn ecn_alpha_fast_path_large_frac() {\n        let mut s = make_state();\n        s.ecn_alpha = 400;\n        s.ecn_ect1 = 0;\n        s.ecn_ce = 0;\n        // delta_ce = 600, delta_ect1 = 400 → frac = 600*1024/(600+400) = 614\n        // frac (614) > alpha (400) and frac >= 512 → fast path: alpha = frac\n        s.ecn_alpha_update_counts(400, 600);\n        assert_eq!(s.ecn_alpha, 614);\n    }\n\n    #[test]\n    fn ecn_alpha_ewma_path() {\n        let mut s = make_state();\n        s.ecn_alpha = 256;\n        s.ecn_ect1 = 0;\n        s.ecn_ce = 0;\n        // delta_ce = 100, delta_ect1 = 900 → frac = 100*1024/1000 = 102\n        // frac (102) < alpha (256) → EWMA path\n        // alpha_shifted = 256 * 16 - 256 + 102 = 256*15 + 102 = 3840 + 102 = 3942\n        // new alpha = 3942 / 16 = 246\n        s.ecn_alpha_update_counts(900, 100);\n        assert_eq!(s.ecn_alpha, 246);\n    }\n\n    #[test]\n    fn ecn_alpha_only_ect1_delta() {\n        let mut s = make_state();\n        s.ecn_alpha = 200;\n        s.ecn_ect1 = 0;\n        s.ecn_ce = 0;\n        // delta_ect1 = 500, delta_ce = 0 → frac = 0\n        // frac (0) < alpha (200) → EWMA:\n        //   alpha_shifted = 200 << 4 = 3200; 3200 - 200 = 3000; 3000 + 0 = 3000\n        //   new alpha = 3000 >> 4 = 187\n        s.ecn_alpha_update_counts(500, 0);\n        assert_eq!(s.ecn_alpha, 187);\n    }\n}\n","numLines":530,"startLine":1,"totalLines":530}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_016KA97U5pBYTz3kfnL2xH6X","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a clear picture of what needs to be implemented. Let me also check what helper functions are needed in bbr1.rs:\n\n1. **`picoquic_bbr1_reset`** (bbr1.c:449-467) - already has `suspension_almost_over` and `suspension_exit` methods, but I need to add `reset` method\n2. **`picoquic_bbr1_notify_congestion`** (bbr1.c:1118-1157) - needs `notify_congestion` method\n3. **`picoquic_bbr1_notify`** (bbr1.c:1191-1319) - needs `notify` function\n\n\n4. For the reset function, I can leverage the existing `set_options`, `enter_startup`, `set_send_quantum`, and `update_target_cwnd` methods that are already implemented.\n5. For the notify function, I need to identify what `picoquic_cc_get_sequence_number` and `picoquic_cc_hystart_loss_test` do and whether they need to be implemented as well.\n\nNow I'm working through the remaining dependencies for the notify function—checking which helper functions like `picoquic_cc_hystart_test`, `picoquic_cc_slow_start_increase`, `PICOQUIC_BYTES_FROM_RATE`, `picoquic_update_pacing_data`, `picoquic_update_pacing_rate`, and `BBR1SetPacingRate` already exist in the Rust implementation or need to be ported over.\n\nI also need to examine `picoquic_bbr1_notify_congestion` which calls `BBR1ExitStartupLongRtt` and `picoquic_cc_get_sequence_number`, and check the cc_common.rs file for any shared helper functions.\n\nFor the `bytestream_vint_len` function, I can see it's just wrapping the varint length calculation, so I'll need to add a standalone helper that matches the existing `ByteStream::varint_encoded_len` functionality.\n\nNow looking at the `c4_delay_threshold` function, I need to understand how it calculates the delay threshold using sensitivity and the nominal max RTT, then I need to find what `C4_DELAY_THRESHOLD_MAX` is set to in c4.c.","signature":""}],"stop_reas