{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MQby36MsRAj9axrsAzNxSV","type":"tool_result","content":"230\t* loss detection threshold. We want that threshold to be very\n231\t* high at low data rates (lower than 50kB/s), about 2% at\n232\t* high data rate (matching the sensitivity of BBR), and \n233\t* about 5% at intermediate rates (1MBps), with slopes\n234\t* in between. We assume that the loss threshold is computed as:\n235\t*\n236\t* Threshold = 2% + (1-sensitivity)*50%\n237\t* \n238\t* This gives us the curve points:\n239\t* - 0 to 50kB/s: 0\n240\t* - 1MB/s: (1-0.03/0.5) = 0.94, approximate to 963/1024\n241\t* - 10MB/s: 1\n242\t*/\n243\t\n244\tstatic uint64_t c4_sensitivity_1024(c4_state_t* c4_state)\n245\t{\n246\t    uint64_t sensitivity = 1024;\n247\t    if (c4_state->nominal_rate < 50000) {\n248\t        sensitivity = 0;\n249\t    }\n250\t    else if (c4_state->nominal_rate > 10000000) {\n251\t        sensitivity = 1024;\n252\t    }\n253\t    else if (c4_state->nominal_rate < 1000000) {\n254\t        sensitivity = (c4_state->nominal_rate - 50000) * 963 / 950000;\n255\t    }\n256\t    else {\n257\t        sensitivity = 963 + ((c4_state->nominal_rate - 1000000) * 61 / 9000000);\n258\t    }\n259\t    return sensitivity;\n260\t}\n261\t\n262\t/* Compute the delay threshold for declaring congestion,\n263\t* as the min of RTT/8 and c4_DELAY_THRESHOLD_MAX (25 ms) \n264\t */\n265\t\n266\tuint64_t c4_delay_threshold(c4_state_t* c4_state)\n267\t{\n268\t    uint64_t sensitivity = c4_sensitivity_1024(c4_state);\n269\t    uint64_t fraction = 64 + MULT1024(1024 - sensitivity, 196);\n270\t    uint64_t delay = MULT1024(fraction, c4_state->nominal_max_rtt);\n271\t    if (delay > C4_DELAY_THRESHOLD_MAX) {\n272\t        delay = C4_DELAY_THRESHOLD_MAX;\n273\t    }\n274\t    return delay;\n275\t}\n276\t\n277\t/* Compute the ECNmarking threshold for declaring a congestion event.\n278\t* The marking threshold should be large if the sensitivity is small --\n279\t* maybe 25%, and smaller if the sensitivity is large -- maybe 12.5%.\n280\t*/\n281\tuint64_t c4_ecn_threshold(c4_state_t* c4_state)\n282\t{\n283\t    uint64_t sensitivity = c4_sensitivity_1024(c4_state);\n284\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"36feb9dd-a64c-482f-8d2d-3dfde6f4c9e3","uuid":"343319b0-b51d-429f-8645-0387998e438f","timestamp":"2026-05-07T13:39:32.396Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/richbarn/Projects/picoquic/picoquic/c4.c","content":"* loss detection threshold. We want that threshold to be very\n* high at low data rates (lower than 50kB/s), about 2% at\n* high data rate (matching the sensitivity of BBR), and \n* about 5% at intermediate rates (1MBps), with slopes\n* in between. We assume that the loss threshold is computed as:\n*\n* Threshold = 2% + (1-sensitivity)*50%\n* \n* This gives us the curve points:\n* - 0 to 50kB/s: 0\n* - 1MB/s: (1-0.03/0.5) = 0.94, approximate to 963/1024\n* - 10MB/s: 1\n*/\n\nstatic uint64_t c4_sensitivity_1024(c4_state_t* c4_state)\n{\n    uint64_t sensitivity = 1024;\n    if (c4_state->nominal_rate < 50000) {\n        sensitivity = 0;\n    }\n    else if (c4_state->nominal_rate > 10000000) {\n        sensitivity = 1024;\n    }\n    else if (c4_state->nominal_rate < 1000000) {\n        sensitivity = (c4_state->nominal_rate - 50000) * 963 / 950000;\n    }\n    else {\n        sensitivity = 963 + ((c4_state->nominal_rate - 1000000) * 61 / 9000000);\n    }\n    return sensitivity;\n}\n\n/* Compute the delay threshold for declaring congestion,\n* as the min of RTT/8 and c4_DELAY_THRESHOLD_MAX (25 ms) \n */\n\nuint64_t c4_delay_threshold(c4_state_t* c4_state)\n{\n    uint64_t sensitivity = c4_sensitivity_1024(c4_state);\n    uint64_t fraction = 64 + MULT1024(1024 - sensitivity, 196);\n    uint64_t delay = MULT1024(fraction, c4_state->nominal_max_rtt);\n    if (delay > C4_DELAY_THRESHOLD_MAX) {\n        delay = C4_DELAY_THRESHOLD_MAX;\n    }\n    return delay;\n}\n\n/* Compute the 